{
  "requirement": "`selector` addresses the item and `kind` describes it. `span` is a half-open byte range in the retained source. `structural_hash` identifies the item’s outline-relevant contents.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct OutlineItem {\n    pub selector: String,\n    pub kind: String,\n    pub span: Range<usize>,\n    pub structural_hash: String,\n}\n\nimpl OutlineItem {\n    pub fn new(\n        selector: String,\n        kind: String,\n        span: Range<usize>,\n        structural_hash: String,\n    ) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl Clone for OutlineItem;\nimpl Debug for OutlineItem;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject `requirements.sdk.outlines.OutlineItem` is mostly a declared API contract. It has four public fields, a `new` constructor, `#[non_exhaustive]`, and `Clone` and `Debug` impls. Its prose adds meanings for `selector`, `kind`, `span` and `structural_hash`.\n\nThe marked test is `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]`. It runs `cargo doc`, then calls `documented_exports` and `check_declaration` for every exported item. For `OutlineItem`, `check_declaration` does the following:\n- It reads the requirement text from `md/requirements/sdk/outlines.md` and takes the `rust,ignore` declaration and the trait-implementation block.\n- It compares `signature_parts` of the requirement's declaration with the rustdoc declaration. A changed field name or type, a changed `new` signature, or an extra or missing public member would fail.\n- It asserts that a struct with public fields carries `#[non_exhaustive]`.\n- It compares the trait implementations listed in the requirement (`Clone`, `Debug`) with those rustdoc reports. A missing `Clone` or `Debug`, or an extra impl, would fail.\n- It checks that the requirement has descriptive prose.\n\nThe helper `member_order_is_free_but_field_and_method_types_are_committed` shows that the comparison is sensitive to field and method types.\n\nTogether these checks cover the obligations the subject states about shape. They are the field set and types, the `new` signature, `non_exhaustive`, and the trait impls.\n\nThe meanings of `span` and `structural_hash` are produced by the outline-building code. Sibling requirements specify how that code derives them: the \"Inspect selectable items\" and \"Fingerprint\" sections of `md/requirements/sdk/outlines.md`, and the per-language fingerprint chapters. Those requirements own their tests, so they are not reassessed here.\n\n`OutlineItem::new` only stores its arguments. It has no conditional and no transformation, so it qualifies for the pass-through exemption. `tests/outline_content.rs` also constructs items with `new`, though it has no `{test}` reference to the subject.\n\nI found no behavior in the subject that the reviewed tests would accept while violating it, and no acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "34070f30c190da855a0af0db8758db88cea74ad388475c8cd2f1dfaa1fb9eb00",
